94139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410140 1078 #edb/ref 17592186410124 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410140 1079 #uuid "f7c5ef5b-7a80-5ac2-99a7-b5d9b6b74e69" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410141 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410139 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410141 1069 "q-183471" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410141 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410141 1071 "Negate the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ At least one prime number is even." 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410141 1072 #uuid "1b470ce3-7367-5e3f-ae84-b975432e9387" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410141 1074 "Let $P$ be the set of all prime numbers. The given statement can be re-phrased as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exists $p\\in P$ such that $p$ is even.\n\nIntroducing the existential quantifier, we get the following:\n\n$\\,$ $∃p\\in P,\\,p\\text{ is even}.$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∃p\\in P,\\,p\\text{ is even}) & ≡∀p\\in P,\\,¬(p\\text{ is even}) \\\\  & ≡∀p\\in P,\\,p\\text{ is odd}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich reads \n\n$\\,$ For all $p\\in P,$ $p$ is odd.\n\nor simply\n\n$\\,$ Every prime number is odd." 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410142 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410136 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410142 1069 "q-183455" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410142 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410142 1071 "Negate the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ For all $i\\in Z,$ $5∤i.$\n\n*Hint: Recall that $a∣b$ means \"$a$ divides $b.$\"*" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410142 1072 #uuid "4e77b832-cd26-598b-a9cd-768bdf101358" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410142 1074 "If we denote\n\n$$\nP(i):5∣i,\n$$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀i\\in Z,\\,¬P(i).\n$$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∀i\\in Z,\\,¬P(i)) & ≡∃i\\in Z,\\,¬¬P(i) \\\\  & ≡∃i\\in Z,\\,\\text{ }P(i).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $∃i\\in Z,\\,P(i)$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **There exists** $i\\in Z$ such that $5∣i.$" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410143 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410138 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410143 1069 "q-216686" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410143 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410143 1071 "Negate the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ There exists $k\\in Z$ such that $2k$ is not even." 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410143 1072 #uuid "798a00fa-243f-50df-8297-ecf784686589" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410143 1074 "If we denote\n\n$$\nP(k):2k\\text{ is even},\n$$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∃k\\in Z,\\,¬P(k).\n$$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∃k\\in Z,\\,¬P(k)) & ≡∀k\\in Z,\\,¬¬P(k) \\\\  & ≡∀k\\in Z,\\,P(k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $∀k\\in Z,\\,P(k)$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **For all** $k\\in Z,$ $2k$ is even." 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410144 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410137 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410144 1069 "q-183651" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410144 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410144 1071 "Negate the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ Some rational numbers are not proper fractions." 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410144 1072 #uuid "b61a6bc3-02ad-503d-9726-3870de55612a" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410144 1074 "The given statement can be re-phrased as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exists $x\\in Q$ such that $x$ is not a proper fraction.\n\nIntroducing the existential quantifier, we get the following:\n\n$\\,$ $∃x\\in Q,\\,x\\text{ is not a proper fraction}.$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∃x\\in Q,\\,x\\text{ is not a proper fraction}) & ≡∀x\\in Q,\\,¬(x\\text{ is not a proper fraction}) \\\\  & ≡∀x\\in Q,\\,x\\text{ is a proper fraction}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich reads \n\n$\\,$ For all $x\\in Q,$ $x\\text{ is a proper fraction}.$\n\nor simply\n\n$\\,$ All rational numbers are proper fractions." 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410145 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410140 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410145 1069 "q-216590" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410145 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410145 1071 "Negate the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ For all $m\\in N,$ $3m+1$ is not odd." 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410145 1072 #uuid "c83b3bea-4b77-5cec-bbd2-330b49e09c81" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410145 1074 "If we denote\n\n$$\nP(m):3m+1\\text{ is odd},\n$$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀m\\in N,\\,¬P(m).\n$$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∀m\\in N,\\,¬P(m)) & ≡∃m\\in N,\\,¬¬P(m) \\\\  & ≡∃m\\in N,\\,P(m).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $∃m\\in N,\\,P(m)$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **There exists** $m\\in N$ such that $3m+1$ is odd." 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410146 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410150 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410146 1062 #uuid "572c75d6-a924-55fc-82ec-9c67ff02ed45" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410146 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410142 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410147 1062 #uuid "8695aa81-39f5-5e81-8b64-009141aabaf1" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410147 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410143 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410148 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410149 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410148 1062 #uuid "e053a657-a0c4-5b0c-be02-023521cbea13" 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410148 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410144 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410149 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410147 13194139533590 17592186045417 true] [17592186410149 1062 #uuid "e973016a-86f0-5ff0-b7fb-787bf770612e" 1319413